WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:05.961
Captain's Log, Stardate 45959.1.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:08.234
The Enterprise
has been recalled

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.765
to Sector 001
on a priority mission.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.404
All we've been told is that
evidence has been discovered

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:16.643
indicating the presence
of extraterrestrials on Earth

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.275
five centuries ago.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:21.287
Work crews were down here
installing seismic regulators

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.949
when they found some
remarkable artifacts.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:24.979
And it's been determined

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.992
that they date back
to the late 19th century?

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.187
Yes.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.263
Ah.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.858
The bifocal visual aid
is typical of the era.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:41.668
The weapon is a.45 caliber
double-action cavalry pistol

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:44.973
invented by Colt Firearms
in 1873.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.036
Here, look inside the watch.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.481
Hmm.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.751
What makes you think
that extraterrestrials

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.485
are related
to these discoveries?

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:01.392
The crew was having a problem
with the regulators.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.895
Something inside the cavern

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.295
was interfering
with the phase conditioners.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.390
It turned out to be
the cavern itself.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:18.842
The composition of the rock face
has been altered

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.176
by exposure to triolic waves.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.341
Which you're not going
to find on Earth

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.613
in either the 19th
or 24th century.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.279
Triolic waves?

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.117
The by-product
of an energy source

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.713
employed by very few species

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:33.555
because of its deleterious
effect on living tissue.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.720
We've confirmed that no one

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:38.925
has been in or out
of this cavern in centuries.

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:41.957
So we're left with
a 500-year-old mystery.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.798
I'm curious, Doctor.

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:45.805
There are far greater experts
on Earth

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.329
to investigate your mystery.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.568
Why bring the Enterprise
all the way home?

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.577
As we continued our excavation

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.842
we found one other thing
I haven't shown you yet.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:58.180
We've tried to leave everything
as we found it.

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:40.758
Space, the final frontier.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:44.627
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.632
Its continuing mission...

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:50.602
to explore strange new worlds

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:55.005
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:02:55.107 --> 00:03:00.010
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:03:56.167 --> 00:04:00.604
Captain's Log, Stardate 45960.2.

00:04:00.638 --> 00:04:02.538
We have transported
the materials

00:04:02.573 --> 00:04:05.736
discovered in the cavern
back to the ship for analysis.

00:04:05.777 --> 00:04:08.245
I wish I could be
as dispassionate

00:04:08.279 --> 00:04:11.407
about the implications
as my Second Officer.

00:04:11.449 --> 00:04:13.076
Interesting.

00:04:13.117 --> 00:04:16.177
There is a 12% decomposition
of bitanium

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:17.619
in the neural pathway links.

00:04:17.655 --> 00:04:20.089
That suggests that
the alloys are vulnerable...

00:04:20.124 --> 00:04:22.786
Data, how can you
look inside that...

00:04:22.827 --> 00:04:25.591
analyze the decomposition
without...?

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:26.688
Emotion, sir?

00:04:26.731 --> 00:04:27.925
Yes.

00:04:27.966 --> 00:04:30.434
I am simply trying to make
an objective assessment.

00:04:30.468 --> 00:04:32.095
Data, is this yours?

00:04:32.136 --> 00:04:33.262
I believe so, sir.

00:04:33.304 --> 00:04:35.431
Could it be Lore?

00:04:35.473 --> 00:04:37.839
No, sir. My brother's
positronic brain

00:04:37.875 --> 00:04:38.842
has a type "L"

00:04:38.876 --> 00:04:40.935
phase-discriminating
amplifier.

00:04:40.979 --> 00:04:42.776
Mine is a type "R."

00:04:42.814 --> 00:04:44.281
Type "R"?

00:04:44.315 --> 00:04:45.782
Yes, sir.

00:04:45.817 --> 00:04:48.445
Can you predict how long
this has been in the cavern?

00:04:48.486 --> 00:04:50.954
The decomposition
strongly indicates

00:04:50.989 --> 00:04:53.787
that life was terminated
approximately 500 years ago.

00:04:53.825 --> 00:04:54.985
That would be consistent

00:04:55.093 --> 00:04:56.993
with the other artifacts
we recovered.

00:04:57.095 --> 00:04:59.222
Your head is not an artifact.

00:04:59.263 --> 00:05:00.890
In relative terms, perhaps not.

00:05:00.932 --> 00:05:02.365
Nevertheless, it seems clear

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.868
that my life is to end
in the late 19th century.

00:05:04.902 --> 00:05:06.096
Not if we can help it.

00:05:06.137 --> 00:05:08.503
There is no way
anyone can prevent it, sir.

00:05:08.539 --> 00:05:09.699
At some future date

00:05:09.741 --> 00:05:12.733
I will be transported
back to 19th-century Earth

00:05:12.777 --> 00:05:14.210
where I will die.

00:05:14.245 --> 00:05:16.076
It has occurred.

00:05:16.114 --> 00:05:17.945
It will occur.

00:05:17.982 --> 00:05:21.247
Well, I can't tell you
exactly who the aliens were

00:05:21.285 --> 00:05:24.186
but I have found out
a few things.

00:05:28.826 --> 00:05:30.953
The triolicized rock face
tells us

00:05:31.029 --> 00:05:33.725
that we're probably dealing
with a species

00:05:33.765 --> 00:05:35.892
with microcentrum
cell membranes.

00:05:35.933 --> 00:05:37.594
Triolic waves
wouldn't harm them.

00:05:37.635 --> 00:05:39.262
It also might mean

00:05:39.303 --> 00:05:40.964
they're shape-shifters
of some kind.

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:43.132
So they could have appeared
on Earth as humans.

00:05:43.174 --> 00:05:45.608
I don't think it's anybody
we've ever run into before.

00:05:45.643 --> 00:05:48.271
Nothing we've found matches up
with any known life-forms.

00:05:48.312 --> 00:05:51.577
What does match up
is a cellular fossil

00:05:51.616 --> 00:05:54.244
which might have been
along just for the ride.

00:05:54.285 --> 00:05:56.219
A cellular fossil?

00:05:56.254 --> 00:05:57.881
A microscopic
ciliated life-form

00:05:57.922 --> 00:06:00.948
not unlike a thousand other
single cell life-forms

00:06:00.992 --> 00:06:03.153
you'd find
on any planet surface.

00:06:03.194 --> 00:06:06.186
Except this particular one
is L-B-10445

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:11.395
and L-B-10445 is only known
to exist on one place...

00:06:11.436 --> 00:06:14.269
Devidia II in the Marrab sector.

00:06:14.305 --> 00:06:16.899
Number One, lay in a course.

00:06:16.941 --> 00:06:18.602
On my way.

00:06:30.521 --> 00:06:33.490
So, do you want
to talk about it?

00:06:33.524 --> 00:06:35.151
Are you referring

00:06:35.193 --> 00:06:37.423
to the foreknowledge
of my death?

00:06:37.462 --> 00:06:39.089
Yeah.

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:41.894
I have no particular desire
to discuss the matter.

00:06:41.933 --> 00:06:43.730
Do you need to talk about it?

00:06:43.768 --> 00:06:45.235
Yeah.

00:06:45.269 --> 00:06:46.736
Ah. Why?

00:06:46.771 --> 00:06:49.672
Data, this has got
to bother you a little.

00:06:49.707 --> 00:06:52.699
On the contrary,
I find it rather comforting.

00:06:52.743 --> 00:06:54.210
Comforting?

00:06:54.245 --> 00:06:56.736
I have often wondered
about my own mortality

00:06:56.781 --> 00:06:58.908
as I have seen others
around me age.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:01.145
Until now, it has been
theoretically possible

00:07:01.185 --> 00:07:03.915
that I would live
an unlimited period of time

00:07:04.021 --> 00:07:06.455
and although some might
find this attractive

00:07:06.491 --> 00:07:08.459
to me it only reinforces

00:07:08.493 --> 00:07:11.189
the fact that I am...
artificial.

00:07:11.229 --> 00:07:13.891
I never knew how tough
this must be for you.

00:07:13.931 --> 00:07:15.228
Tough?

00:07:15.266 --> 00:07:16.597
As in difficult?

00:07:16.634 --> 00:07:20.536
Knowing that you would
outlive all your friends.

00:07:20.571 --> 00:07:23.199
I expected to make new friends.

00:07:23.241 --> 00:07:24.868
True.

00:07:24.909 --> 00:07:27.742
And then to outlive
them as well.

00:07:27.778 --> 00:07:30.406
Now that you know
that you might not?

00:07:30.448 --> 00:07:33.576
It provides a sense
of completion to my future.

00:07:33.618 --> 00:07:36.587
In a way, I am not that
different from anyone else.

00:07:36.621 --> 00:07:39.249
I can now look forward to death.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:41.758
I never thought of it that way.

00:07:41.792 --> 00:07:43.589
One might also conclude

00:07:43.628 --> 00:07:46.722
that it brings me one step
closer to being human.

00:07:46.764 --> 00:07:48.231
I am mortal.

00:07:48.266 --> 00:07:50.063
Picard to Bridge officers.

00:07:50.101 --> 00:07:52.569
We're approaching
the Devidia system.

00:07:52.603 --> 00:07:54.230
Report to your stations.

00:07:54.272 --> 00:07:55.637
I'll see you later.

00:07:55.673 --> 00:07:58.403
Let's get together for a game
of chess or something, okay?

00:08:01.045 --> 00:08:04.037
That sounded like
a very intense discussion.

00:08:04.081 --> 00:08:08.450
Yeah, they found Data's head
a mile beneath San Francisco.

00:08:08.486 --> 00:08:11.284
Been down there
about five centuries.

00:08:11.322 --> 00:08:14.917
That's why the Enterprise
is being sent back to Earth.

00:08:14.959 --> 00:08:16.620
I didn't realize.

00:08:16.661 --> 00:08:18.322
Something, isn't it?

00:08:19.564 --> 00:08:21.794
He seems fine about it.

00:08:21.832 --> 00:08:24.460
Better than I am.

00:08:24.502 --> 00:08:27.938
Well, I'd better get
to Engineering.

00:08:27.972 --> 00:08:30.736
Full circle.

00:08:30.775 --> 00:08:32.436
Hmm.

00:08:34.779 --> 00:08:36.371
I heard about Data.

00:08:36.414 --> 00:08:38.041
Yeah.

00:08:38.082 --> 00:08:41.916
It's having an unusually
traumatic effect on everyone.

00:08:41.953 --> 00:08:43.580
Yeah.

00:08:43.621 --> 00:08:46.749
If you don't want
to talk about it, it's okay.

00:08:46.791 --> 00:08:48.418
I'm fine. I'm just...

00:08:48.459 --> 00:08:50.086
Angry.

00:08:50.127 --> 00:08:51.754
I'm not angry.

00:08:51.796 --> 00:08:54.458
Yeah, I'm angry.

00:08:56.434 --> 00:08:58.959
Why should I be angry?

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:02.369
Maybe because it reminds us
of our own mortality.

00:09:02.406 --> 00:09:04.101
I just don't want
to believe it.

00:09:04.141 --> 00:09:07.042
Have you ever heard Data
define friendship?

00:09:07.078 --> 00:09:08.705
No.

00:09:08.746 --> 00:09:10.714
How did he put it?

00:09:10.748 --> 00:09:15.208
"As I experience certain
sensory input patterns

00:09:15.253 --> 00:09:18.381
"my mental pathways
become accustomed to them.

00:09:18.422 --> 00:09:21.323
"The inputs eventually
are anticipated

00:09:21.359 --> 00:09:23.293
and even missed when absent."

00:09:23.327 --> 00:09:25.557
So what's the point?

00:09:25.596 --> 00:09:27.223
He's used to us

00:09:27.265 --> 00:09:29.062
and we're used to him.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.568
It's like finding out
someone you love

00:09:31.602 --> 00:09:33.536
has a terminal illness...

00:09:33.571 --> 00:09:34.868
Data.

00:09:34.905 --> 00:09:36.429
Counselor.

00:09:36.474 --> 00:09:38.101
Commander.

00:09:45.783 --> 00:09:50.243
Would either of you mind
if I made a personal inquiry?

00:09:50.288 --> 00:09:51.915
A personal inquiry?

00:09:51.956 --> 00:09:53.583
No, go right ahead.

00:09:53.624 --> 00:09:55.922
I am perceiving
an apparent change

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:58.656
in the way
others behave toward me.

00:09:58.696 --> 00:10:02.757
For example, people abruptly
end conversations when I appear

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:06.099
just as you did
when the turbolift doors opened.

00:10:06.137 --> 00:10:08.435
Is that
an accurate observation?

00:10:08.472 --> 00:10:11.100
- Not at all.
- Yes.

00:10:11.142 --> 00:10:12.769
Yes.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:14.437
You're right, Data

00:10:14.478 --> 00:10:17.777
and it's not
a very nice thing to do.

00:10:17.815 --> 00:10:20.443
It's just that
our mental pathways

00:10:20.484 --> 00:10:24.113
have become accustomed
to your sensory input patterns.

00:10:24.155 --> 00:10:25.782
Hmm.

00:10:25.823 --> 00:10:27.450
I understand.

00:10:27.491 --> 00:10:30.119
I am also fond of you,
Commander

00:10:30.161 --> 00:10:32.493
and you as well, Counselor.

00:10:50.815 --> 00:10:52.442
We're in orbit.

00:10:52.483 --> 00:10:54.144
Any sign of life?

00:10:54.185 --> 00:10:55.652
Negative, sir.

00:10:55.686 --> 00:10:59.747
Captain, sensors are picking up
an unusual temporal disturbance

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:02.759
on a small area
of the planet's surface.

00:11:02.793 --> 00:11:06.593
42 degrees, seven minutes north
by 88 degrees, declination east.

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:08.427
Temporal disturbance?

00:11:08.466 --> 00:11:11.765
Put us in the standard orbit
above those coordinates.

00:11:11.802 --> 00:11:14.327
Spectral analysis shows
a high level of triolic waves

00:11:14.372 --> 00:11:15.930
emanating
from the same location.

00:11:15.973 --> 00:11:17.372
Any correlation
with the readings

00:11:17.408 --> 00:11:18.375
we received from Earth?

00:11:18.409 --> 00:11:19.376
Affirmative, sir.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:20.536
The magnetic signature

00:11:20.578 --> 00:11:22.170
is identical to the one
found in the cavern.

00:11:22.213 --> 00:11:24.306
Could those triolic waves
be dangerous for humanoids?

00:11:24.348 --> 00:11:25.975
Only with
long-term exposure, sir.

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.210
There is no immediate threat.

00:11:27.251 --> 00:11:28.618
Take an away team.

00:11:28.751 --> 00:11:31.720
Worf, Geordi, Troi, join me
in Transporter Room Three

00:11:31.754 --> 00:11:32.778
for an away team.

00:11:32.822 --> 00:11:34.119
Commander?

00:11:34.156 --> 00:11:37.819
Mr. Data, I'll need your help
to monitor the sensor readings

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:39.851
during this investigation.

00:11:42.465 --> 00:11:45.992
Captain, may I speak
to you alone?

00:11:51.507 --> 00:11:54.999
Sir, it is standard procedure

00:11:55.111 --> 00:11:57.909
that the second officer
accompany the away team.

00:11:57.947 --> 00:12:00.006
Yes, yes, Mr. Data,
I am aware of that.

00:12:00.082 --> 00:12:02.710
Then I must assume
your decision is related

00:12:02.752 --> 00:12:03.946
to the discovery on Earth...

00:12:03.986 --> 00:12:06.181
I think it is reasonable
to take precautions.

00:12:06.222 --> 00:12:08.383
Captain, there is

00:12:08.424 --> 00:12:10.221
no rational justification
for this course.

00:12:10.259 --> 00:12:12.318
Then I'll be irrational.

00:12:15.297 --> 00:12:16.423
It is possible, sir

00:12:16.465 --> 00:12:18.490
that the events
leading to my death

00:12:18.534 --> 00:12:19.967
will not occur for years

00:12:20.036 --> 00:12:21.594
even centuries.

00:12:21.637 --> 00:12:23.264
I hope that's true, Mr. Data.

00:12:23.305 --> 00:12:26.274
Nevertheless, this investigation
began with your death.

00:12:26.308 --> 00:12:29.744
I'm simply trying to see
that it doesn't end that way.

00:12:29.779 --> 00:12:32.441
I appreciate your concern,
Captain

00:12:32.481 --> 00:12:36.212
but to employ an aphorism,
one cannot "cheat fate."

00:12:36.252 --> 00:12:39.153
Cheat fate?

00:12:41.357 --> 00:12:43.587
Perhaps we can't, Mr. Data

00:12:43.626 --> 00:12:46.754
but at least
we can give it a try.

00:13:05.214 --> 00:13:06.408
Hmm...

00:13:08.451 --> 00:13:10.544
The concentration
of triolic waves

00:13:10.586 --> 00:13:12.110
falls off about here.

00:13:12.154 --> 00:13:13.485
Mm-hmm.

00:13:17.226 --> 00:13:20.195
It increases exponentially
the closer in we go.

00:13:20.229 --> 00:13:23.824
What's the source...
something underground?

00:13:23.866 --> 00:13:25.265
Negative, Commander.

00:13:25.301 --> 00:13:26.529
What's the explanation?

00:13:26.569 --> 00:13:27.968
I don't have one yet.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.367
La Forge to Enterprise.

00:13:29.405 --> 00:13:30.429
Go ahead.

00:13:30.473 --> 00:13:32.338
Data, run a spectral
field correlation for me.

00:13:32.374 --> 00:13:33.966
Let's find out if these
triolic readings

00:13:34.076 --> 00:13:34.974
are in any way related

00:13:35.077 --> 00:13:37.443
to the temporal distortions.

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:39.880
Acknowledged.

00:13:39.915 --> 00:13:41.906
Deanna?

00:13:45.955 --> 00:13:47.547
There's life here.

00:13:51.293 --> 00:13:55.992
A child, an old woman...

00:13:56.098 --> 00:13:58.692
dozens more, hundreds.

00:13:58.734 --> 00:14:00.668
Terrified.

00:14:00.703 --> 00:14:02.568
Terrified?

00:14:05.641 --> 00:14:09.099
My God, Will, they're human.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:21.187
Whatever they are,
Troi's convinced they're human.

00:14:21.223 --> 00:14:22.850
They may be trapped somehow.

00:14:22.892 --> 00:14:23.950
We're not sure.

00:14:24.059 --> 00:14:25.959
Captain, the results
of my temporal analysis

00:14:26.061 --> 00:14:26.959
may be pertinent.

00:14:27.062 --> 00:14:27.960
Go ahead.

00:14:28.063 --> 00:14:30.088
Geordi, it indicates
a synchronic distortion

00:14:30.132 --> 00:14:31.827
in the areas emanating
triolic waves.

00:14:31.867 --> 00:14:33.960
Well, that explains
a few things.

00:14:34.036 --> 00:14:35.663
How much, Data?

00:14:35.704 --> 00:14:40.505
A positive displacement
of.004%.

00:14:40.543 --> 00:14:43.535
Well, whatever
or whoever is there

00:14:43.579 --> 00:14:44.637
we're out of phase with it

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:47.274
but we're only talking
by a fraction of a second.

00:14:47.316 --> 00:14:50.149
A fraction of a second
would make them invisible?

00:14:50.186 --> 00:14:53.485
A millisecond, a year...
it wouldn't make any difference.

00:14:53.522 --> 00:14:54.887
If what we're reading is true

00:14:54.924 --> 00:14:56.551
then we're occupying
the same space

00:14:56.592 --> 00:14:57.752
but in a different time.

00:14:57.793 --> 00:14:59.226
How do we compensate?

00:14:59.261 --> 00:15:01.161
Commander, we might be able

00:15:01.197 --> 00:15:03.358
to manipulate
the synchronic distortion.

00:15:03.399 --> 00:15:04.491
Maybe.

00:15:04.533 --> 00:15:07.366
If we were to create a contained
subspace force field.

00:15:07.403 --> 00:15:09.166
But to get a.004 variance

00:15:09.205 --> 00:15:10.832
we'd need an incredibly
sensitive

00:15:10.873 --> 00:15:12.204
phase discriminator, Data.

00:15:12.241 --> 00:15:14.539
I don't think we have one
that would even come close.

00:15:14.577 --> 00:15:15.737
Yes, we do.

00:15:15.778 --> 00:15:18.804
It is built
into my positronic decompiler.

00:15:18.848 --> 00:15:22.011
It will be necessary for me
to join the away team, sir.

00:15:27.223 --> 00:15:29.384
Proceed, Mr. Data.

00:15:42.471 --> 00:15:43.529
Mr. Data.

00:15:43.572 --> 00:15:44.539
Sir.

00:15:44.573 --> 00:15:47.337
Let me give you
a hand with that, Data.

00:15:47.376 --> 00:15:49.537
Once I have adjusted
the force field

00:15:49.578 --> 00:15:51.637
I will no longer be
visible, Commander.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.580
I have taken steps
however to ensure

00:15:53.616 --> 00:15:55.709
that you will still
be able to hear me.

00:15:55.751 --> 00:15:58.447
If you will assist me
in a test of the com system.

00:15:58.487 --> 00:15:59.977
My voice will be transmitted

00:16:00.089 --> 00:16:02.649
on a delay correlated
to the phase adjustment.

00:16:02.691 --> 00:16:05.216
That should allow me
to maintain verbal contact.

00:16:05.261 --> 00:16:06.853
Will we be able
to talk to you?

00:16:06.896 --> 00:16:07.863
No, sir.

00:16:07.897 --> 00:16:09.455
That will not be possible.

00:16:11.467 --> 00:16:13.867
The subspace field
has been established.

00:16:13.903 --> 00:16:16.701
You're set to go, Data.

00:16:16.739 --> 00:16:20.869
Adjusting
the synchronic distortion:

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:23.310
.001.

00:16:23.345 --> 00:16:26.075
.002.

00:16:26.115 --> 00:16:29.084
.003.

00:16:29.118 --> 00:16:32.110
.004.

00:16:35.324 --> 00:16:37.918
I have made visual contact.

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:40.861
There are life-forms here.

00:16:40.896 --> 00:16:45.196
They are either unaware of me
or choosing to ignore me.

00:16:45.234 --> 00:16:47.702
I am moving approximately
ten meters north

00:16:47.736 --> 00:16:50.796
of my starting position
to observe more closely.

00:16:50.839 --> 00:16:54.468
They range from two
to three meters in height

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:56.068
silver-gray in color.

00:16:56.111 --> 00:16:57.738
They have four limbs.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:59.873
No eyes or ears are noticeable.

00:16:59.915 --> 00:17:01.849
There is a single orifice

00:17:01.884 --> 00:17:05.081
where a humanoid forehead
would ordinarily be.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:07.145
They are reclined
against the rock face

00:17:07.189 --> 00:17:09.555
surrounding an apparatus
of some sort

00:17:09.591 --> 00:17:12.560
approximately 1.5 meters
in height.

00:17:12.594 --> 00:17:14.425
It is releasing

00:17:14.463 --> 00:17:16.829
what appear to be
energy fragments

00:17:16.865 --> 00:17:19.231
which are then ingested
by the entities

00:17:19.268 --> 00:17:20.633
through the orifice

00:17:20.669 --> 00:17:23.263
perhaps
some sort of nourishment.

00:17:23.305 --> 00:17:25.068
The upper portion
of the apparatus

00:17:25.107 --> 00:17:27.940
seems to be a holding facility
for the energy segments.

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:30.205
There are hundreds,
perhaps thousands

00:17:30.245 --> 00:17:31.872
of these fragments inside.

00:17:31.914 --> 00:17:35.042
I have resumed
a northerly direction.

00:17:35.084 --> 00:17:38.053
There is no evidence yet
of humans.

00:17:38.087 --> 00:17:39.645
Okay, that's enough, Data.

00:17:39.688 --> 00:17:41.246
Come on back now.

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:43.884
I have encountered

00:17:43.926 --> 00:17:47.054
another life-form...
an ophidian.

00:17:47.096 --> 00:17:51.055
It seems to be restricted
by a force field.

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:54.797
Two of the silver-gray entities
are approaching it.

00:17:54.837 --> 00:17:56.828
They have released
the force field.

00:17:59.108 --> 00:18:01.668
I am reading
a temporal distortion...

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:03.610
of... mass... ortions...

00:18:03.645 --> 00:18:04.873
the ophidian is...

00:18:04.913 --> 00:18:06.744
...time-space continuum...

00:18:06.782 --> 00:18:08.249
...caught in
the after effect...

00:18:08.283 --> 00:18:10.080
...I am attempting...

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:12.212
Data!

00:18:14.757 --> 00:18:16.725
Over here.

00:18:16.759 --> 00:18:18.784
Commander Riker, report.

00:18:22.131 --> 00:18:24.122
We've lost him.

00:18:56.998 --> 00:18:58.022
Excuse me.

00:19:00.401 --> 00:19:01.663
Uh, pardon me.

00:19:01.703 --> 00:19:04.797
I am searching
for two individuals

00:19:04.839 --> 00:19:07.273
with an ophidian.

00:19:07.308 --> 00:19:08.707
A snake.

00:19:10.812 --> 00:19:12.302
Frenchmen!

00:19:14.315 --> 00:19:16.306
Hmm.

00:19:32.867 --> 00:19:36.166
Could you help out
a '49er?

00:19:36.204 --> 00:19:39.105
I-I-I fell down a shaft.

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:41.768
I got blown up in a tunnel.

00:19:41.809 --> 00:19:43.367
That is unfortunate.

00:19:43.411 --> 00:19:45.379
It is most unfortunate.

00:19:45.413 --> 00:19:48.940
I require large amounts
of whiskey as a liniment.

00:19:48.983 --> 00:19:52.146
I am sorry, but I have
no whiskey to give you.

00:19:52.186 --> 00:19:53.813
I'll take a dime.

00:19:53.855 --> 00:19:57.450
I am sorry, but I have
no form of legal tender.

00:19:57.492 --> 00:20:00.222
Oh. We're in the same boat, huh?

00:20:00.261 --> 00:20:02.229
Well, this is my street.

00:20:02.263 --> 00:20:05.824
You'll have to go
find one of your own.

00:20:05.867 --> 00:20:08.631
I would be happy to do so

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:11.696
but I am presently
in search of information.

00:20:11.739 --> 00:20:14.606
Oh. Stockbrokers
are cheap as hell.

00:20:14.642 --> 00:20:16.610
Don't even bother to ask.

00:20:16.644 --> 00:20:17.804
Your best handout

00:20:17.845 --> 00:20:21.178
is from a young fella
with his lady.

00:20:21.215 --> 00:20:25.413
You give him a chance
to show her he's generous.

00:20:25.453 --> 00:20:27.318
Steer clear of sailors.

00:20:27.355 --> 00:20:29.585
Most likely you'll get

00:20:29.624 --> 00:20:33.219
a fist across your jaw
for your trouble.

00:20:33.261 --> 00:20:35.229
Thank you for your advice

00:20:35.263 --> 00:20:38.824
but I am trying to find
two individuals with a snake.

00:20:38.866 --> 00:20:40.595
A snake?

00:20:40.635 --> 00:20:43.502
You are an odd fellow,
aren't you?

00:20:43.538 --> 00:20:48.703
But just don't be too particular
where you get your funds from.

00:20:50.344 --> 00:20:53.108
You are in need
of medical attention.

00:20:53.147 --> 00:20:55.115
I will get a doctor.

00:20:55.149 --> 00:20:56.309
No, no, no.

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:58.318
It's too late for that.

00:20:58.352 --> 00:20:59.683
Oh!

00:20:59.721 --> 00:21:02.383
Could you help out a '49er?

00:21:12.366 --> 00:21:14.960
Thanks.

00:21:17.505 --> 00:21:19.871
Hey. Put it on Gentleman Jim.

00:21:19.907 --> 00:21:21.397
Knockout in the fifth.

00:21:21.442 --> 00:21:22.409
All right.

00:21:22.443 --> 00:21:25.241
Sir, I need temporary lodging.

00:21:25.279 --> 00:21:27.406
Looks like the missus
booted you out

00:21:27.448 --> 00:21:29.075
in the middle of the night.

00:21:31.119 --> 00:21:33.417
Ah, I understand the source
of your misperception.

00:21:33.454 --> 00:21:35.422
However, this is not sleepwear

00:21:35.456 --> 00:21:37.720
and I do not have a missus.

00:21:37.759 --> 00:21:38.987
Well...

00:21:39.026 --> 00:21:40.493
I am a Frenchman.

00:21:40.528 --> 00:21:41.552
Oh.

00:21:41.596 --> 00:21:43.154
Well, everybody's
from somewhere.

00:21:43.197 --> 00:21:45.165
Now, that doesn't matter
at this hotel.

00:21:45.199 --> 00:21:47.224
It's six bits a day
or four dollars a week.

00:21:47.268 --> 00:21:49.634
I have no money.

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:50.830
Oh, well, now that matters.

00:21:50.872 --> 00:21:53.966
But I am capable of performing
significant tasks

00:21:54.008 --> 00:21:55.839
both mental and physical.

00:21:55.877 --> 00:21:58.846
Perhaps your hotel
would offer me a job.

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.006
Jeez, I don't know.

00:22:00.047 --> 00:22:02.345
We're pretty happy
with the maid we've got.

00:22:02.383 --> 00:22:03.543
The cook's decent.

00:22:03.584 --> 00:22:05.211
The dishwasher's drunk all day...

00:22:05.253 --> 00:22:07.949
but at least
he gets here on time...

00:22:08.055 --> 00:22:09.454
and, uh, there's me.

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:10.821
I do everything else
around here.

00:22:10.858 --> 00:22:11.950
Sorry.

00:22:12.059 --> 00:22:16.428
Lady luck not
with you tonight, Mr. Lane?

00:22:16.464 --> 00:22:17.556
Poor fellow.

00:22:17.598 --> 00:22:20.590
Hasn't filled a straight
in five weeks.

00:22:20.635 --> 00:22:23.627
Poker?

00:22:31.746 --> 00:22:33.941
Fold.

00:22:33.981 --> 00:22:36.211
Me, too.

00:22:41.489 --> 00:22:43.081
Go to blazes.

00:22:44.192 --> 00:22:48.492
A poker face carved in marble.

00:22:48.529 --> 00:22:50.087
Excuse me, gentlemen.

00:22:50.131 --> 00:22:52.099
What in hell do you want?

00:22:52.133 --> 00:22:54.363
I would like to join the game.

00:22:54.402 --> 00:22:57.496
Pale face.

00:22:57.538 --> 00:23:00.006
I don't like easterners,
personally.

00:23:00.041 --> 00:23:01.941
I am a Frenchman.

00:23:01.976 --> 00:23:07.141
Ah, mes parents
sont originaires de Bourgogne.

00:23:07.181 --> 00:23:10.309
Je suis ne a la New Orleans.

00:23:10.351 --> 00:23:12.683
Alors, nous sommes
presque freres.

00:23:12.720 --> 00:23:15.052
Je suis heureux
de vous connaitre.

00:23:17.325 --> 00:23:19.555
Please, sir.

00:23:24.098 --> 00:23:25.861
The game is poker.

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:28.095
The deal is yours.

00:23:28.135 --> 00:23:31.070
The ante is four bits.

00:23:36.744 --> 00:23:38.268
Family heirloom?

00:23:38.312 --> 00:23:40.280
In a manner of speaking.

00:23:40.314 --> 00:23:42.714
It is a crystalline composite

00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:45.241
of silicon, beryllium,
carbon 70 and...

00:23:45.286 --> 00:23:46.253
Gold.

00:23:46.287 --> 00:23:47.276
Gold.

00:23:54.295 --> 00:23:57.093
I'll give you
three dollars for it.

00:23:59.100 --> 00:24:01.091
I accept.

00:24:12.480 --> 00:24:14.414
Did you see the looks
on their faces?

00:24:14.448 --> 00:24:16.609
I did everything I could
not to laugh.

00:24:16.651 --> 00:24:18.619
To whom are you referring?

00:24:18.653 --> 00:24:20.553
Frederick La Rouque
and Joe Falling Hawk.

00:24:20.588 --> 00:24:22.715
Those guys are card sharks.

00:24:22.757 --> 00:24:25.487
Sure, they, uh, play easy at
first not to scare off the marks

00:24:25.526 --> 00:24:29.963
but you give them a little time,
they'll bleed a man dry

00:24:30.064 --> 00:24:33.500
especially a, uh,
out-of-towner like yourself.

00:24:33.534 --> 00:24:36.162
What was the source
of your jocular reaction?

00:24:39.407 --> 00:24:41.204
What was it you found humorous?

00:24:41.242 --> 00:24:42.300
Oh, don't you see?

00:24:42.343 --> 00:24:44.106
They had you pegged for a sap.

00:24:44.145 --> 00:24:46.636
The clothes you got on,
the way you talk...

00:24:46.681 --> 00:24:49.206
it's like you
were born yesterday.

00:24:49.250 --> 00:24:51.218
You sure fooled them though.

00:24:51.252 --> 00:24:53.379
It was not my intention
to deceive.

00:24:53.421 --> 00:24:54.683
Well, have it your way.

00:24:54.722 --> 00:24:55.689
This is the place.

00:24:55.723 --> 00:24:57.350
Uh, breakfast is 6:00 to 8:00.

00:24:57.391 --> 00:25:00.019
Check-out's at noon
when you're ready to leave.

00:25:01.329 --> 00:25:02.694
Thank you.

00:25:03.965 --> 00:25:06.331
It has been a pleasure.

00:25:06.367 --> 00:25:07.561
Ahem!

00:25:07.601 --> 00:25:11.367
It would be advisable
to monitor that cough.

00:25:11.405 --> 00:25:13.896
I have read that there is
currently a cholera epidemic

00:25:13.941 --> 00:25:15.533
in San Francisco.

00:25:15.576 --> 00:25:17.339
Never felt better.

00:25:17.378 --> 00:25:19.369
Ahem.

00:25:20.548 --> 00:25:22.140
Of course.

00:25:22.183 --> 00:25:24.651
The gratuity.

00:25:24.685 --> 00:25:26.653
Thank you for your assistance.

00:25:26.687 --> 00:25:27.711
A dollar?

00:25:27.755 --> 00:25:29.723
If there's anything
you need...

00:25:29.757 --> 00:25:31.657
It can get Ionely
in San Francisco.

00:25:31.692 --> 00:25:33.660
You might want some company.

00:25:33.694 --> 00:25:35.753
I can introduce
you to... Lillian.

00:25:35.796 --> 00:25:38.094
I have no need
for companionship.

00:25:38.132 --> 00:25:40.100
However, I do require
some supplies.

00:25:40.134 --> 00:25:42.898
Anything you need...
I can get it for you wholesale.

00:25:42.937 --> 00:25:46.429
I can get it for you
less than wholesale

00:25:46.474 --> 00:25:49.568
if you don't ask me
where it came from.

00:25:49.610 --> 00:25:51.805
What do you need
all this stuff for?

00:25:51.846 --> 00:25:53.711
I am an inventor.

00:25:53.748 --> 00:25:54.874
No kidding.

00:25:54.915 --> 00:25:57.645
Well, this stuff's going
to take awhile.

00:25:57.685 --> 00:26:00.415
I'll have to go
clear across town.

00:26:00.454 --> 00:26:02.251
And it's not going to be cheap.

00:26:04.392 --> 00:26:06.360
Will this be enough?

00:26:06.394 --> 00:26:08.225
More than enough.

00:26:08.262 --> 00:26:11.322
You may retain
the surplus for yourself.

00:26:11.365 --> 00:26:12.662
Keep the change?

00:26:12.700 --> 00:26:13.928
Exactly.

00:26:14.001 --> 00:26:15.059
Done.

00:26:24.712 --> 00:26:27.545
Help out a '49er.

00:26:27.581 --> 00:26:31.540
Fell down... a shaft.

00:26:35.056 --> 00:26:37.388
'49er...

00:26:41.829 --> 00:26:43.660
Help me.

00:26:48.669 --> 00:26:51.866
Help me out.

00:26:55.676 --> 00:27:00.010
No. No.

00:27:17.264 --> 00:27:19.391
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:27:19.433 --> 00:27:20.900
Close-range sensor analysis

00:27:20.934 --> 00:27:24.062
has yielded no further trace
of Commander Data.

00:27:24.104 --> 00:27:27.403
Despite the emotional
repercussions among my crew

00:27:27.441 --> 00:27:29.341
I must move
this mission forward.

00:27:29.376 --> 00:27:31.469
I'm not willing to accept
that he's dead

00:27:31.511 --> 00:27:32.910
and just leave it at that.

00:27:32.946 --> 00:27:34.573
We cannot make
Mr. Data our priority.

00:27:34.615 --> 00:27:36.105
What is more
important than Data?

00:27:36.149 --> 00:27:38.140
Look at what we have so far...

00:27:38.185 --> 00:27:39.709
evidence that these aliens

00:27:39.753 --> 00:27:41.948
have been traveling
in time to Earth.

00:27:41.989 --> 00:27:43.217
What if they're trying

00:27:43.257 --> 00:27:45.555
to undermine our history
for some reason?

00:27:45.592 --> 00:27:47.287
Some kind of guerrilla war?

00:27:47.327 --> 00:27:50.262
We must assume that
there is a threat.

00:27:50.297 --> 00:27:52.663
If not to us, then
to 19th-century Earth.

00:27:52.699 --> 00:27:55.065
We have to determine
what that threat may be.

00:27:55.102 --> 00:27:56.660
Mr. La Forge, we have
to find some way

00:27:56.703 --> 00:27:58.261
to communicate
with these life-forms.

00:27:58.305 --> 00:28:01.001
It's not going to be easy
to reproduce what Data did.

00:28:01.041 --> 00:28:03.202
We can create
a contained subspace field

00:28:03.243 --> 00:28:06.610
but we'd need an extraordinarily
sensitive phase discriminator

00:28:06.647 --> 00:28:08.205
to get that.004 variance.

00:28:08.248 --> 00:28:09.408
Can you build one?

00:28:11.285 --> 00:28:13.185
Won't be as good as Data's.

00:28:13.220 --> 00:28:14.847
Will it be good enough?

00:28:14.888 --> 00:28:16.185
I don't know.
I can try.

00:28:16.223 --> 00:28:17.690
It's going to take
some time, though.

00:28:17.724 --> 00:28:19.851
I don't want anyone else
going in alone.

00:28:19.893 --> 00:28:22.361
I can probably create
a large enough subspace field

00:28:22.396 --> 00:28:24.193
to encompass everyone.

00:28:24.231 --> 00:28:25.926
But adjusting the phase
inside the field

00:28:26.033 --> 00:28:27.557
that's going to be
the hard part.

00:28:27.601 --> 00:28:28.966
Make it so.

00:28:29.970 --> 00:28:31.665
We have to assume
one thing, sir.

00:28:31.705 --> 00:28:32.729
Wherever Data may be

00:28:32.773 --> 00:28:34.536
he's doing the same
thing we are...

00:28:34.574 --> 00:28:36.940
which is trying to get
to the bottom of this.

00:28:36.977 --> 00:28:38.069
He may have a better idea

00:28:38.111 --> 00:28:39.578
about what's going on
than we do.

00:28:39.613 --> 00:28:41.080
So it might be
in the best interest

00:28:41.114 --> 00:28:42.342
of this mission to find him.

00:28:42.382 --> 00:28:45.681
Perhaps in the course of
this investigation we will.

00:28:45.719 --> 00:28:46.947
I hope so.

00:28:47.054 --> 00:28:49.249
If we find Commander Data

00:28:49.289 --> 00:28:52.918
it may be our fate
to die with him in the past.

00:28:52.960 --> 00:28:55.428
If our remains
are in that cavern

00:28:55.462 --> 00:28:58.556
they would have turned
to dust long ago.

00:29:12.412 --> 00:29:14.642
I'm afraid to interrupt.

00:29:14.681 --> 00:29:15.909
Captain...

00:29:15.949 --> 00:29:18.179
you didn't have to come
all the way down here.

00:29:18.218 --> 00:29:19.810
I would have been
more than happy

00:29:19.853 --> 00:29:21.013
to have come up to you.

00:29:21.054 --> 00:29:22.646
And miss all this?

00:29:22.689 --> 00:29:25.783
I haven't seen
such a complex operation

00:29:25.826 --> 00:29:29.125
since the Academy lab final
in exochemistry.

00:29:29.162 --> 00:29:31.756
It's a Tzartak aperitif.

00:29:31.798 --> 00:29:33.527
It's very, very touchy.

00:29:33.567 --> 00:29:36.127
The trick is to change
the evaporation point

00:29:36.169 --> 00:29:37.796
of the main ingredient.

00:29:37.838 --> 00:29:41.330
You want the temperature
where the liquid goes to vapor

00:29:41.375 --> 00:29:42.865
to be a half a degree below

00:29:42.909 --> 00:29:44.604
the body temperature
of the customer.

00:29:44.644 --> 00:29:47.772
That way, when the liquid
touches the tongue

00:29:47.814 --> 00:29:50.942
it evaporates,
and the flavor is carried

00:29:51.051 --> 00:29:52.746
entirely by the vapor.

00:29:52.786 --> 00:29:54.219
A few molecules off

00:29:54.254 --> 00:29:57.655
the vapor point crashes,
and poof... it's all gone.

00:29:57.691 --> 00:29:59.352
All of it.

00:30:00.761 --> 00:30:04.197
What is it you wanted
to see me about?

00:30:04.231 --> 00:30:06.563
I hear you're sending
an away team

00:30:06.600 --> 00:30:07.931
down to the surface.

00:30:07.968 --> 00:30:09.435
Uh-huh.

00:30:09.469 --> 00:30:11.596
Are you going?

00:30:11.638 --> 00:30:14.402
Well, now,
this is rather unusual

00:30:14.441 --> 00:30:17.899
for you to be curious
about an away mission.

00:30:17.944 --> 00:30:21.107
Maybe it's
an unusual away mission.

00:30:21.148 --> 00:30:25.278
If you have something to say,
I'm listening.

00:30:25.318 --> 00:30:29.618
Starfleet captains don't usually
accompany away teams.

00:30:29.656 --> 00:30:32.625
It's general policy.

00:30:32.659 --> 00:30:34.991
This time you have to.

00:30:35.062 --> 00:30:36.996
Why?

00:30:37.097 --> 00:30:40.624
You just do.

00:30:44.971 --> 00:30:47.997
Do you remember
the first time we met?

00:30:48.075 --> 00:30:49.838
Of course.

00:30:49.876 --> 00:30:52.709
Don't be so sure.

00:30:52.746 --> 00:30:54.839
I just mean

00:30:54.881 --> 00:30:58.715
if you don't go
on this mission...

00:31:01.588 --> 00:31:04.386
we'll never meet.

00:31:30.484 --> 00:31:32.975
Oh. Whoo.

00:31:33.053 --> 00:31:35.487
Sorry it took so long, Mr. Data.

00:31:35.522 --> 00:31:37.752
An apology is not necessary.

00:31:37.791 --> 00:31:39.759
Whoo.

00:31:39.793 --> 00:31:41.761
Whoa... hey...

00:31:41.795 --> 00:31:43.422
Ow.

00:31:43.463 --> 00:31:44.987
Are you all right?

00:31:45.065 --> 00:31:48.000
I believe I have
overexerted myself.

00:31:48.068 --> 00:31:50.502
Yeah, I'll say.

00:31:50.537 --> 00:31:52.334
Did you get it working?

00:31:52.372 --> 00:31:53.498
Yes.

00:31:53.540 --> 00:31:55.007
Whatever it is.

00:31:55.075 --> 00:31:56.508
This is for your trouble.

00:31:56.543 --> 00:31:58.943
What are you going
to do with the anvil?

00:31:58.979 --> 00:32:01.948
I require a low-intensity
magnetic field core.

00:32:01.982 --> 00:32:05.543
I believe the iron mass
of the anvil will provide that.

00:32:05.585 --> 00:32:08.884
Well, uh, what's it gonna be
when it's finished?

00:32:08.922 --> 00:32:12.289
What do you think
it is... gonna be?

00:32:12.325 --> 00:32:14.293
If I were to guess?

00:32:14.327 --> 00:32:16.795
Maybe a, uh, a new kind of motor

00:32:16.830 --> 00:32:19.060
for one of those
horseless carriages.

00:32:19.099 --> 00:32:20.964
That is a good guess.

00:32:21.001 --> 00:32:22.093
Hot damn.

00:32:22.135 --> 00:32:24.729
You really think there's
money in those things?

00:32:24.771 --> 00:32:26.068
Perhaps.

00:32:26.106 --> 00:32:28.574
Isn't that what makes
America great?

00:32:28.608 --> 00:32:31.577
To what are you referring?

00:32:31.611 --> 00:32:33.977
Well, a man rides into town
in his pajamas

00:32:34.014 --> 00:32:36.278
wins a grub stake
at a poker table

00:32:36.316 --> 00:32:38.580
turns it
into a horseless carriage

00:32:38.618 --> 00:32:40.677
and makes a million bucks?
That's America.

00:32:40.720 --> 00:32:43.746
I believe I have given you
an erroneous impression.

00:32:43.790 --> 00:32:48.193
You know,
someday my ship's gonna come in.

00:32:48.228 --> 00:32:49.855
You have a ship?

00:32:49.896 --> 00:32:51.363
Oh, yeah.

00:32:51.398 --> 00:32:53.366
And it's full of gold, too.

00:32:53.400 --> 00:32:55.732
I'm just biding my time
till it gets here

00:32:55.769 --> 00:32:57.498
raising a stake any way I can.

00:32:57.537 --> 00:32:59.903
I've been a newsie,
cut fish at a cannery

00:32:59.940 --> 00:33:02.534
heck, I've even been
an oyster pirate.

00:33:02.576 --> 00:33:05.568
You have had a considerable
spectrum of occupations.

00:33:05.612 --> 00:33:08.479
Well, you can't stay
in one place too long.

00:33:08.515 --> 00:33:10.949
I'm always looking
for the angle, you know.

00:33:11.017 --> 00:33:14.680
Say, maybe you and I could go
into business together

00:33:14.721 --> 00:33:16.518
selling your horseless
carriage and all.

00:33:16.556 --> 00:33:19.150
You invent 'em, I sell 'em.

00:33:19.192 --> 00:33:21.353
I can sell anybody anything.

00:33:21.394 --> 00:33:23.055
What do you say?

00:33:24.097 --> 00:33:27.362
I believe your plan
is a bit premature.

00:33:28.868 --> 00:33:31.735
Well, keep it in mind though.

00:33:31.771 --> 00:33:33.705
I better get back.

00:33:34.874 --> 00:33:36.501
Oh, I forgot.

00:33:36.543 --> 00:33:39.410
I got you something
at the bakery on third.

00:33:39.446 --> 00:33:40.913
Oh.

00:33:40.947 --> 00:33:42.414
Thank you, Jack.

00:33:42.449 --> 00:33:43.916
Oh, no, no, no.

00:33:43.950 --> 00:33:46.214
It's on me...
partner.

00:34:08.274 --> 00:34:13.075
The eminent scientist
Alfred Russell Wallace

00:34:13.113 --> 00:34:14.944
has revived the theory

00:34:15.015 --> 00:34:19.349
that Earth is at the center
of the stellar universe.

00:34:22.055 --> 00:34:24.387
This, uh...

00:34:24.424 --> 00:34:26.392
distinguished...

00:34:26.426 --> 00:34:29.054
natural...

00:34:29.095 --> 00:34:31.393
philosopher...

00:34:31.431 --> 00:34:36.232
has, uh, reaffirmed our planet

00:34:36.269 --> 00:34:40.865
as the only habitable globe
in the heavens.

00:34:40.907 --> 00:34:42.898
A world, furthermore

00:34:42.942 --> 00:34:46.878
constructed for the sole benefit
of man.

00:34:46.913 --> 00:34:48.107
Hmm.

00:34:49.949 --> 00:34:53.612
He's got a lot of folks
excited about the notion.

00:34:53.653 --> 00:34:55.211
My dear, Mr. Clemens

00:34:55.255 --> 00:34:58.224
why do I think
you're not one of them?

00:34:58.258 --> 00:35:00.283
Your suspicions,
Madame Guinan

00:35:00.326 --> 00:35:01.384
are undoubtedly based

00:35:01.428 --> 00:35:04.261
upon your keen
observational skills.

00:35:06.266 --> 00:35:08.427
Now, if you'll permit me

00:35:08.468 --> 00:35:10.265
I'll continue

00:35:10.303 --> 00:35:13.101
my character assassination
unimpeded.

00:35:13.139 --> 00:35:17.542
My dear, Mr. Clemens,
please do, please do.

00:35:17.577 --> 00:35:21.536
According to our best
geologic estimate

00:35:21.581 --> 00:35:24.744
the Earth is approximately
100 million years of age.

00:35:24.784 --> 00:35:27.344
Perhaps it is less,
perhaps more.

00:35:27.387 --> 00:35:29.150
Perhaps a great deal more.

00:35:29.189 --> 00:35:31.180
Indeed.

00:35:31.224 --> 00:35:33.784
But regardless, it is ancient...

00:35:33.827 --> 00:35:36.921
in the extreme.

00:35:36.963 --> 00:35:41.866
Now, geology also tells us
that man himself has existed

00:35:41.901 --> 00:35:45.894
but for a microscopic fraction
of those years.

00:35:49.542 --> 00:35:51.908
Curious, isn't it?

00:35:51.945 --> 00:35:56.348
That the world got by
for such a great long while

00:35:56.382 --> 00:36:02.218
with no humans around
to fill up space.

00:36:02.255 --> 00:36:06.783
I suppose Mr. Wallace
and his supporters would say

00:36:06.826 --> 00:36:09.920
that the Earth needed
all that time

00:36:09.963 --> 00:36:13.831
to prepare itself
for our illustrious arrival.

00:36:13.867 --> 00:36:15.835
Why...

00:36:15.869 --> 00:36:18.531
the oyster alone

00:36:18.571 --> 00:36:22.632
probably required
15 million years

00:36:22.675 --> 00:36:25.337
to get it to come out
just right.

00:36:26.646 --> 00:36:29.046
But if the Earth is not alone

00:36:29.082 --> 00:36:30.276
and there are millions

00:36:30.316 --> 00:36:32.375
of inhabited planets
in the heavens...

00:36:32.418 --> 00:36:34.045
Quite my point.

00:36:34.087 --> 00:36:38.183
Man becomes a trivial creation,
does he not?

00:36:38.224 --> 00:36:42.558
Lost in the vastness
of the cosmic prairie

00:36:42.595 --> 00:36:47.089
adrift on the deep ocean
of time.

00:36:47.133 --> 00:36:49.863
A single one amongst...

00:36:50.870 --> 00:36:52.963
...countless others.

00:36:53.006 --> 00:36:56.772
Some may argue that a diamond
is still a diamond

00:36:56.809 --> 00:36:59.972
even if it is one
amongst millions.

00:37:00.046 --> 00:37:02.480
It still shines as brightly.

00:37:02.515 --> 00:37:05.211
Someone might say that,
dear lady

00:37:05.251 --> 00:37:07.219
if someone thought

00:37:07.253 --> 00:37:11.053
that the human race
was akin to a precious jewel.

00:37:13.326 --> 00:37:18.525
But this increasingly
hypothetical someone

00:37:18.565 --> 00:37:20.624
would not be me.

00:37:24.437 --> 00:37:26.098
Good afternoon, sir.

00:37:26.139 --> 00:37:27.606
Good afternoon.

00:37:27.640 --> 00:37:29.904
I would like to speak
to Guinan.

00:37:29.943 --> 00:37:31.570
And you are?

00:37:31.611 --> 00:37:33.238
Data.

00:37:33.279 --> 00:37:34.746
Mr. Data...

00:37:34.781 --> 00:37:37.306
Could it be under another name?

00:37:37.350 --> 00:37:38.647
No.

00:37:38.685 --> 00:37:40.812
I can't seem to find your name
on the guest list, sir.

00:37:40.853 --> 00:37:42.548
I am a personal friend.

00:37:42.589 --> 00:37:44.386
Madame Guinan
has discovered

00:37:44.424 --> 00:37:46.358
many personal friends

00:37:46.392 --> 00:37:48.690
since the newspaper
announcement

00:37:48.728 --> 00:37:50.696
but if your name is
not on the guest list

00:37:50.730 --> 00:37:51.890
there's nothing I can do.

00:37:51.931 --> 00:37:53.523
It is urgent
that I speak to her.

00:37:53.566 --> 00:37:56.467
Sir, unless you leave
this house immediately

00:37:56.502 --> 00:37:58.527
I will send for the police.

00:37:58.571 --> 00:38:00.368
That is an excellent idea.

00:38:00.406 --> 00:38:02.636
I will wait for them
in there.

00:38:02.675 --> 00:38:05.235
Sir, please,
you can't go in there.

00:38:05.278 --> 00:38:06.438
Guinan!

00:38:08.314 --> 00:38:10.578
I must speak to you immediately.

00:38:10.617 --> 00:38:12.414
Forgive me, madam,
he just barged right in.

00:38:12.452 --> 00:38:14.818
I am sorry for the disruption,
but he would not believe me

00:38:14.854 --> 00:38:17.118
when I told him
we were friends.

00:38:17.156 --> 00:38:19.556
Do I know you, Mr...?

00:38:19.592 --> 00:38:21.583
...Data. Yes.

00:38:21.628 --> 00:38:24.256
We were on a ship together.

00:38:24.297 --> 00:38:26.527
Well, I do so much traveling.

00:38:26.566 --> 00:38:28.431
What ship would that be?

00:38:28.468 --> 00:38:30.368
The Enterprise.

00:38:30.403 --> 00:38:31.927
Is that a clipper ship?

00:38:32.005 --> 00:38:34.030
It is a starship.

00:38:34.073 --> 00:38:36.132
Starship?
What registry would that be?

00:38:36.175 --> 00:38:37.802
Of course!

00:38:37.844 --> 00:38:39.505
Mr. Data.

00:38:39.545 --> 00:38:41.172
Excuse us...

00:38:41.214 --> 00:38:43.842
We have so much to catch up on.

00:38:43.883 --> 00:38:45.180
Excuse us.

00:38:45.218 --> 00:38:46.879
Just... how are you?

00:38:50.390 --> 00:38:52.187
What exactly are you?

00:38:52.225 --> 00:38:53.852
Android.

00:38:53.893 --> 00:38:55.520
Artificial life-form.

00:38:55.561 --> 00:38:57.188
Ah...

00:38:57.230 --> 00:38:58.697
Did my father send you here?

00:38:58.731 --> 00:39:00.528
Because if he did,
you must go back

00:39:00.566 --> 00:39:02.534
and tell him I'm not
done listening...

00:39:02.568 --> 00:39:04.126
I was not sent by your father.

00:39:04.170 --> 00:39:05.194
Circumstances demand

00:39:05.238 --> 00:39:07.069
that I take you
into my confidence.

00:39:07.106 --> 00:39:09.165
I require your assistance.

00:39:09.208 --> 00:39:11.176
Sorry.

00:39:11.210 --> 00:39:12.404
I am from the 24th century

00:39:12.445 --> 00:39:14.379
where you and I serve
aboard a starship.

00:39:15.615 --> 00:39:16.582
And?

00:39:16.616 --> 00:39:18.914
Our ship encountered
a species who appears

00:39:18.985 --> 00:39:21.749
to be threatening
19th-century Earth.

00:39:21.788 --> 00:39:23.722
I investigated
and was inadvertently

00:39:23.756 --> 00:39:25.587
pulled into their
temporal vortex.

00:39:25.625 --> 00:39:27.115
Ah...

00:39:27.160 --> 00:39:29.890
When I saw your photograph
in the newspaper

00:39:29.929 --> 00:39:32.864
I assumed you had joined me
from the future...

00:39:32.899 --> 00:39:34.196
from the Enterprise.

00:39:34.233 --> 00:39:36.224
I knew your species
was long-lived

00:39:36.269 --> 00:39:37.531
but I did not realize

00:39:37.570 --> 00:39:39.629
you had visited
Earth so long ago.

00:39:46.779 --> 00:39:49.475
Eavesdropping is by no means

00:39:49.515 --> 00:39:52.279
a proper activity
for a gentleman.

00:39:52.318 --> 00:39:54.286
Nonetheless...

00:39:54.320 --> 00:39:57.448
the deed is done.

00:40:01.927 --> 00:40:06.227
Captain's Log, Stardate 45965.3.

00:40:06.265 --> 00:40:08.165
An away team has beamed
to the surface

00:40:08.200 --> 00:40:10.794
with a device
which may enable them

00:40:10.836 --> 00:40:14.932
to phase-shift
into the alien world.

00:40:14.973 --> 00:40:17.806
Okay, Counselor,
right over there.

00:40:25.617 --> 00:40:28.518
The triolic waves
end right here.

00:40:31.423 --> 00:40:33.015
Mr. Worf.

00:40:50.275 --> 00:40:51.936
Sir.

00:40:51.977 --> 00:40:54.673
How soon will you be ready?

00:40:54.713 --> 00:40:56.772
We're ready now, Captain.

00:40:58.851 --> 00:41:01.718
The subspace field
is established.

00:41:01.753 --> 00:41:02.947
I'd be more comfortable

00:41:02.988 --> 00:41:05.616
if you'd monitor our progress
from the Bridge, Captain.

00:41:05.657 --> 00:41:06.817
I have reason to believe

00:41:06.859 --> 00:41:08.918
that my presence
on this mission is imperative.

00:41:08.961 --> 00:41:10.428
Imperative?

00:41:10.462 --> 00:41:12.794
Yes. Mr. Worf, you will
report back to the Bridge.

00:41:12.831 --> 00:41:17.564
Sir, as Chief of Security,
my place is at your side.

00:41:17.603 --> 00:41:19.127
The security of the Enterprise

00:41:19.171 --> 00:41:21.071
is of paramount importance,
Mr. Worf.

00:41:22.307 --> 00:41:23.968
Yes, sir.

00:41:25.210 --> 00:41:26.837
Worf to Enterprise.

00:41:26.879 --> 00:41:28.779
Go ahead, sir.

00:41:28.814 --> 00:41:30.406
Beam me up.

00:41:32.317 --> 00:41:34.251
Proceed, Mr. La Forge.

00:41:39.358 --> 00:41:41.223
I've modified this tricorder

00:41:41.260 --> 00:41:43.228
to interface
with the subspace generator.

00:41:43.262 --> 00:41:45.992
It should allow me to control
the phase discrimination...

00:41:46.031 --> 00:41:48.090
assuming this
is going to work at all.

00:41:48.133 --> 00:41:51.000
I'll need everyone
inside the field.

00:42:00.479 --> 00:42:05.314
Adjusting synchronic
distortion... 001.

00:42:07.753 --> 00:42:10.517
.002.

00:42:10.555 --> 00:42:12.785
.003.

00:42:12.824 --> 00:42:16.089
.004.

00:42:26.571 --> 00:42:29.972
If we can see them,
why can't they see us?

00:42:30.075 --> 00:42:32.805
The phase displacement
might not bring us far enough

00:42:32.844 --> 00:42:34.311
into their perceptual range.

00:42:39.451 --> 00:42:42.978
These strands appear to be
biomagnetic, variable flux

00:42:43.055 --> 00:42:45.216
possibly organic in origin.

00:42:45.257 --> 00:42:47.953
A life-form.

00:42:51.129 --> 00:42:53.222
No.

00:42:53.265 --> 00:42:55.199
There's no life here.

00:43:05.277 --> 00:43:09.145
What I have sensed
is more like an imprint...

00:43:11.783 --> 00:43:15.378
an echo of the last moment
of life.

00:43:17.923 --> 00:43:19.720
Human life.

00:43:21.960 --> 00:43:24.360
They all died in terror.

00:43:43.281 --> 00:43:44.771
My God.

00:43:46.318 --> 00:43:50.311
They're delivering more of them
for the others to ingest.

00:43:50.355 --> 00:43:53.085
Look at what he's carrying.
